          "Minimizers make the request look small: \"un attimo\", \"solo una domanda veloce\", \"un piccolo favore\". With friends: \"Mi fai un favore?\", \"Ti dispiace se...?\".",
          "Politeness also has to fit the situation. At a bar counter, \"Mi fa un caffè, per favore?\" with the plain present is perfectly polite; \"Le dispiacerebbe prepararmi un caffè?\" would sound ironic. A short apology before the request, \"Scusi il disturbo\" or \"Senta, scusi\", is often enough with strangers. Avoid the calque \"*Posso avere un caffè?\": Italians say \"Mi dà\" or \"Mi fa\", or simply \"Un caffè, per favore\".",
